  "description": "ENUYUI crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C126 H196 Dy6 Ni6 O56 P6,4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Ni1B (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni2B (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni3B (Ni) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.139-3.869 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.98-120.09°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ni6Dy6(OH)2(O3PCH2Ph)6(O2CtBu)16(MeCO2H)2](MeCN)4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
